/-!
# Concrete relabeling data for the Fi₂₃ lift

The label map is the saved simultaneous intertwiner from source labels in
ATLAS F23G1-p31671B0 to ambient labels in F24G1-p306936B0. The two source maps
invert the published right-action cycles, matching `CycleEncoding`.
These definitions assert no comparison with the exact carrier generators.
The separate comparison certificates must establish those equalities.

A balanced tree selects packed blocks of 256 labels, keeping kernel lookup
reductions logarithmic in the number of blocks.
Reproduce with `source/generate.py`; the retained original ATLAS tables and
attribution are in `AtlasCarriers/source/`. Source: GLS3, Table 5.3v.
-/

@[expose] public section
